{
 "about": "The bench's rendered pieces for IR Capture (desktop-bench, branch irkit, helper irkit, 2026-11-03). Sizes in px are the file's pixels; points (pt) are SwiftUI points, px_per_pt says how many of the 1x file's pixels make a point (the @2x file has twice). capInsets are SwiftUI EdgeInsets in points for Image(nsImage:).resizable(capInsets:resizingMode:) on an NSImage whose size is set in points (SwellKit.swift's SwellPictures does it). rects are in the named file's pixels, origin top left.",
 "ref": {
  "window": [
   1440,
   900
  ],
  "frame_k2": 3.2,
  "frame_note": "frame-* pieces: 1 pt = 1 ref px of the bench's 1440x900 layout; the 1x picture has 1.6 px a pt, the @2x 3.2",
  "rack_note": "rack units and the capture player have no fixed point size: 10 pt a cm (the Tools views' scale) makes a 3U rack unit (1128 x 342 px at 22.5 px/cm) 501 x 152 pt; px_per_pt = pxcm / 10"
 },
